<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
	The app's entitlements for the jailbreak wrappers (the deb and the .tipa).
	The ordinary sideload .ipa gets a separate file carrying only the App Group
	(if any): verify-ipa.sh checks jailbreak entitlements for *absence* there
	and for presence here, because the two archives fail in opposite directions.

	`@APP_CLIENT_ENTITLEMENT@` is the private key the daemon's authenticator
	looks for on a peer. Name it after the app, never reuse another app's, and
	never grant it to anything you would not hand a root descriptor to.

	Mach-lookup of `@SERVICE_NAME@` is not optional: without it the app cannot
	find the daemon.

	The App Group is required on the app and every embedded extension that
	shares a container. Delete the key for a Live Activity–only appex, and
	only keep `$(APP_GROUP_IDENTIFIER)` if the packager substitutes it.

	`platform-application` is the default. It attests "signed as platform",
	not "this client". If it is unused on the app, drop it from the app *and*
	from the authenticator together.

	The two storage entitlements are what let the app read other apps' bundles
	and data containers (icons, Info.plist, documents): `no-sandbox` alone does
	not open them on every platform. Keep them on the app *and* on the daemon
	if either one looks there; drop both from an app that has no business
	there.

	`com.apple.security.iokit-user-client-class` names the GPU and what sits
	beside it. Every app carries it, whether or not it draws with Metal
	itself: a bootstrap withholds these IOKit classes from an ad-hoc signed
	binary until they are named, and system frameworks reach for them inside
	the app's process. IconServices composites an app icon through Core
	Image, and Inspector 0.6.2 crashed at launch on an A12 iPhone on iOS 18
	RootHide with a null call in `CI::GLContext::GLContext`, under
	`_applicationIconImageForBundleIdentifier:` (Inspector #15). Bold Text
	does the same through UIKit (Irisin), and so did the share sheet in
	Saily (Irisin #65). A Metal view of the app's own fails without a crash:
	a blank rectangle that never reports a viewport.

	The list is Irisin's: AGX and the older IOAccel names, IOSurface, the
	framebuffer, JPEG decode, HID, `IOGPUDeviceUserClient` and
	`IOAccelerator` from the Bold Text report, the neural engine Vision asks
	for, and vphone's paravirtual names (`AppleParavirt…`,
	`…ParavirtClient`, `AppleVirtIO…`). Both spellings of the key carry the
	same list: the kernel's denial names the plain one, and the Bold Text
	fix was the `exception.` one.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>application-identifier</key>
	<string>@BUNDLE_ID@</string>
	<key>com.apple.security.iokit-user-client-class</key>
	<array>
		<string>AGXCommandQueue</string>
		<string>AGXDevice</string>
		<string>AGXDeviceUserClient</string>
		<string>AGXSharedUserClient</string>
		<string>AGXGLContext</string>
		<string>AppleParavirtDeviceUserClient</string>
		<string>IOAccelerator</string>
		<string>IOAccelContext</string>
		<string>IOAccelContext2</string>
		<string>IOAccelDevice</string>
		<string>IOAccelDevice2</string>
		<string>IOAccelSharedUserClient</string>
		<string>IOAccelSharedUserClient2</string>
		<string>IOAccelSubmitter2</string>
		<string>IOGPUDeviceUserClient</string>
		<string>IOSurfaceRootUserClient</string>
		<string>IOSurfaceAcceleratorClient</string>
		<string>IOSurfaceAcceleratorParavirtClient</string>
		<string>IOMobileFramebufferUserClient</string>
		<string>AppleJPEGDriverUserClient</string>
		<string>H11ANEInDirectPathClient</string>
		<string>AppleVirtIONeuralEngineDeviceUserClient</string>
		<string>IOHIDLibUserClient</string>
		<string>IOHIDEventServiceFastPathUserClient</string>
	</array>
	<key>com.apple.security.exception.iokit-user-client-class</key>
	<array>
		<string>AGXCommandQueue</string>
		<string>AGXDevice</string>
		<string>AGXDeviceUserClient</string>
		<string>AGXSharedUserClient</string>
		<string>AGXGLContext</string>
		<string>AppleParavirtDeviceUserClient</string>
		<string>IOAccelerator</string>
		<string>IOAccelContext</string>
		<string>IOAccelContext2</string>
		<string>IOAccelDevice</string>
		<string>IOAccelDevice2</string>
		<string>IOAccelSharedUserClient</string>
		<string>IOAccelSharedUserClient2</string>
		<string>IOAccelSubmitter2</string>
		<string>IOGPUDeviceUserClient</string>
		<string>IOSurfaceRootUserClient</string>
		<string>IOSurfaceAcceleratorClient</string>
		<string>IOSurfaceAcceleratorParavirtClient</string>
		<string>IOMobileFramebufferUserClient</string>
		<string>AppleJPEGDriverUserClient</string>
		<string>H11ANEInDirectPathClient</string>
		<string>AppleVirtIONeuralEngineDeviceUserClient</string>
		<string>IOHIDLibUserClient</string>
		<string>IOHIDEventServiceFastPathUserClient</string>
	</array>
	<key>com.apple.security.application-groups</key>
	<array><string>$(APP_GROUP_IDENTIFIER)</string></array>
	<key>@APP_CLIENT_ENTITLEMENT@</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.exception.mach-lookup.global-name</key>
	<array>
		<string>@SERVICE_NAME@</string>
	</array>
	<key>com.apple.private.security.no-sandbox</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.private.security.storage.AppBundles</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.private.security.storage.AppDataContainers</key>
	<true/>
	<key>platform-application</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
